      "title": "Block progression when stop-condition evidence becomes unknown",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 212,
      "reason": "Only conditions resolving to true block execution; undefined results are ignored. Reproduced: attest a false stop predicate, change the host environment so its evidence becomes stale, then call nextAction: it returns execute. This violates requirements.md:23 and :29, which require valid condition evidence and investigation of unknown material conditions. Evaluate stop predicates explicitly as three-valued results and return evidence_insufficient for unknown assessments. Validate with stale, missing and unattested stop evidence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "Apply pre-write risk checks to effectful shell operations",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 252,
      "reason": "Pre-write obligations run only when writes() returns true, which excludes request-scoped shell-only operations. Reproduced: supply a trusted, authorized shell request for a local edit and a security risk requiring security-reviewed evidence; without that evidence, nextAction returns execute instead of risk_check. Other branches already recognize shell operations as potentially effectful. Enforce before_write obligations using host-assessed operation effects, conservatively treating potentially mutating operations as effectful. Validate shell-only and destructive-operation requests with missing specialist evidence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Prevent an older pass from masking a current failed check",
      "file": "core.mjs",
      "line": 164,
      "reason": "requirement() accepts any valid passing record without resolving contradictory failures. Reproduced: complete an implementation stage, add a passing behavior-validation test receipt, then add a failed receipt for the same command, cwd, dependencies and environment. evidenceValidity reports the latter as failed, but nextAction returns complete using the older pass. This contradicts requirements.md:23: observed failed checks must not count as success. Introduce explicit check identity and trusted supersession/current-result selection; unresolved contradictory results must block completion. Validate pass→fail and fail→pass sequences."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Audited core.mjs against requirements.md, contracts.md and contracts.skill.yaml; inspected repository instructions and existing-tests.mjs as context. All three axes were evaluated independently; no separate repository-conformance finding. Three issues were reproduced with local, in-memory Node snippets. Receipts were synthetic fixtures, not actual test-command executions. The existing suite was not run because its imports do not resolve. No files were modified; no shell, network or external services were used. Integration validation remains unavailable in this isolated copy."
